        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition>
                "Computing statement trust values based on: (i) provenance information which can be either unknown or a value in the interval [−1,1] where 1: absolute belief, −1: absolute disbelief and 0: lack of belief/ disbelief (ii) opinion-based method, which use trust annotations made by several individuals (iii) provenance information and trust annotations in Semantic Web-based social-networks (iv) annotating triples with provenance data and usage of provenance history to evaluate the trustworthiness of facts."@en ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme>
